#. ja: ドードーネスト
#. de: Dodo-Nest
#. fr: nid de dodo
#. column 2: dodo's nests
#. column 8: Though their beady eyes and awkward walk give them an air of unintelligence, dodos are actually quite clever creatures. A mother dodo will, when creating a nest, first dry grass in the sun for several days before adding it to the pile, so as to prevent the growth of molds harmful to her offspring.
#. column 9: Dodo's Nest
msgctxt "Item:9747:0:0"
msgid "dodo's nest"
msgstr "гнездо додо"

#. de: Dodo-Nester
#. fr: nids de dodo
#. column 0: dodo's nest
#. column 8: Though their beady eyes and awkward walk give them an air of unintelligence, dodos are actually quite clever creatures. A mother dodo will, when creating a nest, first dry grass in the sun for several days before adding it to the pile, so as to prevent the growth of molds harmful to her offspring.
#. column 9: Dodo's Nest
msgctxt "Item:9747:0:2"
msgid "dodo's nests"
msgstr "гнёзда додо"

#. ja: ドードーが卵を孵すための巣
#. de: Obwohl ihre Knopfaugen und ihr ungelenker Gang sie etwas dümmlich erscheinen lassen, sind Dodos in Wirklichkeit ziemlich intelligente Kreaturen. Das Dodo-Weibchen trocknet das beim Nestbau verwendete Gras zunächst für ein paar Tage in der Sonne, damit sich im Nest kein Schimmel bildet, der dem Nachwuchs schaden könnte.
#. fr: Un nid devant permettre à un dodo de pondre ses œufs.
#. column 0: dodo's nest
#. column 2: dodo's nests
#. column 9: Dodo's Nest
msgctxt "Item:9747:0:8"
msgid "Though their beady eyes and awkward walk give them an air of unintelligence, dodos are actually quite clever creatures. A mother dodo will, when creating a nest, first dry grass in the sun for several days before adding it to the pile, so as to prevent the growth of molds harmful to her offspring."
msgstr "Додо кажутся глуповатыми из-за бусинок-глаз и неуклюжей походки, но на самом деле они довольно умны. Перед тем как свить гнездо, самка додо несколько дней сушит траву на солнце, чтобы в ней не завелась плесень, опасная для птенцов."

